# Hugo build output + transient artifacts. The manual is built into public/ at
# build time and embedded into the daemon; the generated site is NOT committed.
# A committed placeholder .gitkeep keeps public/ present so the `manual` package's
# `//go:embed all:public` compiles before Hugo has ever run; `hugo` then populates
# public/ (including index.html) at build time, and none of that output is tracked
# — so a rebuild never shows as a git change. The real page reaches the daemon via
# the build pipeline (task/rpm/release/CI all run `hugo` first), never via a commit.
# A bare `go build` that skips Hugo embeds only .gitkeep, so /manual is empty until
# the manual is built — a deliberate trade for never committing generated HTML.
/public/*
!/public/.gitkeep
/resources/_gen/
.hugo_build.lock
